    "result": "Perfect! The implementation is complete and working correctly. Let me create a concise summary of the changes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval` to fail CI jobs when metrics are too low. Here's what was done:\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli/src/index.ts)\n- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (can be used multiple times)\n- Implemented threshold parsing and validation\n- Validates format (`<metric>=<number>`) and range (0-1)\n- Exits with code 2 for malformed thresholds or unknown metrics\n- Exits with code 1 if any thresholds fail, 0 if all pass\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core/src/eval/index.js)\n- Updated `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter\n- Adds `passed` field and `thresholds` list to reports\n- Properly handles metrics with null scores (fails their thresholds)\n\n### Report Changes (frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js)\n- JSON reports include `passed` and `thresholds` fields\n- Markdown reports include \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status\n\n### Tests & Documentation\n- Added 3 new tests for threshold functionality (all passing)\n- Updated READMEs with usage examples and documentation\n- Included SDK example showing programmatic threshold usage\n\n### Test Results\nExit codes verified:\n- \u2705 Code 0: All thresholds pass\n- \u2705 Code 1: Any threshold fails (report still written)\n- \u2705 Code 2: Usage errors (unknown metric, malformed format, invalid range)\n\nAll requirements are met. Reports and exit codes work correctly with both JSON and Markdown formats.",
